<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="36bd1c3a">&lt;p&gt;
    Effective project standards and procedures save time and establish clear ground rules for the project team. Standards
    are established for time collection, reporting, communications, issue management, scope management, and
    technology/tools.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Project team members will benefit from strong, clearly defined standards. Less rework occurs if practitioners define
    standards before they begin to build deliverables or work products.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Project standards and procedures are highly subjective and variable depending on the type and duration of a project.
    Due to these nuances EY has not defined specific standards or procedures, however the following is a comprehensive
    activity listing for establishing project standards and procedures.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    NOTE: The number of activities listed below that are applicable depend on the size and scope of your project.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Issue Management&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop the issue management procedures
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create an issue worksheet
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create the issue log
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create an issue storage mechanism
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Scope Management&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Establish guidelines and standards for change requests
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Establish the change request evaluation procedures
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create a change request worksheet
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create a change request log
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define how to administer scope updates and change requests
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define the change request reporting requirements
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create a change request storage mechanism
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Quality Management&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Establish deliverable completeness and correctness criteria
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document requirements for metric gathering and analysis tasks
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Appoint a process quality advisor
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document process review task and schedule requirements
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document product review task and schedule requirements
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Risk Management Plan&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop the risk management plan
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop the risk management review requirements
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Knowledge Coordination&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document tool and process for knowledge capture
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document knowledge naming conventions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define the knowledge base views
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define the control structures
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Reporting&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define reporting information needs
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document the reporting cycles and formats
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Communicate reporting standards to the project team
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Project Budget&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Select the information that is required to be collected for the budget
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Establish the information collection frequency (i.e., weekly, monthly, etc.)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Establish the mode of collection for the information (My Business)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document and communicate budget capture procedures
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Project Control File&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Establish document storage/filing system and procedure
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create the electronic project control file
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Contact Directory&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Decide what information should be maintained in the contact directory
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define a collection method for the information
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Distribute and communicate the contact directory
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Technology&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Technology Support&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine the tehnnology-related needs for the project
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Assess the current technology infrastructure in meeting the project needs
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Project Technology Plan&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document the current technology that will support the project needs
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document the hardware that must be obtained
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document the software that must be obtained
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document any additional office equipment that must be obtained
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;u&gt;Hardware and Software&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Obtain the additional hardware and/or software needed to meet the project needs
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Install the hardware and/or software
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
